### evals/files/README.md  [docs]
+ # Eval input files (skill-creator compliant)
+ Place **input files for evals** here. Paths in `evals/evals.json` are relative to the skill root, e.g.:
+ ```json
+ "files": ["evals/files/catalog.csv"]
+ ```
+ - If an eval has no input files, `files` is `[]` and this folder stays empty.
+ - When adding a file, update the corresponding eval entry in `evals/evals.json` with the path under `evals/files/`.

### references/README.md  [docs]
+ # References (skill-creator compliant)
+ This folder contains docs loaded into context **as needed** per the skill-creator anatomy. The main SKILL.md references them with guidance on when to read.
+ | File | When to read |
+ |------|----------------|
+ | [empties_points_guide.md](empties_points_guide.md) | When you need reward catalog templates, empties rules, verification guardrails, or copy examples without re-reading the full SKILL. |
+ Do not load all references by default; use progressive disclosure so only the relevant reference is read for the current task.

### scripts/README.md  [docs]
+ # Scripts (skill-creator compliant)
+ This folder is for **optional executable code** for deterministic or repetitive tasks (per skill-creator anatomy). Currently empty.
+ - If you add scripts (e.g. points liability calculator), document them in SKILL.md with the exact command and when to run them.
+ - Use **forward slashes** in paths (e.g. `scripts/validate.py`), not backslashes.
+ - Scripts can be executed without loading their source into context; the skill only needs to invoke them.